            <div xml:id="d458">

                <pb facs="0491" n="391" xml:id="pg391"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760c.61/215: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wallace</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-21T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 21,
                                1920—2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1391. Reference your telegram no. 1578 of August 19, 5 p.m. If the matter of
                    shipping supplies to Poland should come up for discussion in the Conference of
                    Ambassadors, hope that their transportation may be facilitated may be expressed
                    by you, provided there is a clear understanding that such supplies are to be
                    used only in defending Polish territory and not to make it possible for Poland
                    again to undertake to invade Russia.</p>
                <p>In addition you may state that although the Government of the United States
                    appreciates that it is difficult to effect the transport of munitions with the
                    social conditions which now prevail in Europe, it would be opposed to any
                    efforts to force such transport in opposition to the local or national
                    authorities of the territories through which it is desired to ship the
                    supplies.</p>
                <p>While you may express your views as indicated above, do not take part in giving
                    any instructions to Tower. He is not the agent of the Conference of Ambassadors,
                    but of the League of Nations. Since the United States has not joined the League,
                    it would not be appropriate for this Government to instruct the League
                    representative at the city of Danzig.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
